# Image Asset Workflow

Before building a visually important section, check whether approved real assets exist.

Use:

- `agency/runbooks/image-asset-workflow.md`
- `agency/brief/image-style-guide.md`
- `agency/refs/client-assets.md`, if present
- `agency/refs/live-reference-latest.md`
- Latest reference screenshots

Rules:

- Do not use remote placeholder image services in rendered pages.
- Do not leave broken image URLs.
- Prefer approved local assets from `public/images/{client}/`.
- Harvested client assets in `public/client-assets/source/` are raw source material and must be reviewed before production use.
- If a needed image is missing, create an image brief instead of inventing a random stock-looking placeholder.
- Keep all editable image selections in content JSON. Do not hardcode client-editable image paths in JSX.
